# `for (const character of text)` over 8-bit text is a loop over an index, unrolled four times. No iterator and no one-character string is made:
# `character === ","` loads the byte at the index and compares it with 44. In front of each load stands a test that the piece is one unit long.
# CHECK-LABEL: loop #
# REPEAT: turn = 1..4
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[byte%(turn)]] = Load8Z(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:characters8, {{*}}:StringRangeEqualsLiteral)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@{{*}} = Equal(b@[[byte%(turn)]], $44(
# END REPEAT
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:characters8
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# The patchpoints keep the string alive and are no code.
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 44, patchpoints: 8
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 43, patchpoints: 8
